YUME for Debian
===============

The yume package installs the native YTP/1 client, schema-1 yume-setup and
yume-doctor tools, documentation and examples. The server daemon, /etc/yume,
and disabled systemd unit are in yume-daemon. No service starts on install.

Read /usr/share/doc/yume/QUICKSTART.md and the installed yume/yumed manuals.
Configuration examples are in /usr/share/doc/yume/examples/. Provision a
matching schema-1 kit, validate it and use the config-only native interface:

  yume-doctor --config /path/to/client/yume.json
  yume --config /path/to/client/yume.json --validate
  yume --config /path/to/client/yume.json

For a server, follow /usr/share/doc/yume-daemon/README.Debian. Keep client
credentials off the server.

These development packages are not a frozen ABI or a qualified release.
